== Personal life ==
Byron Donalds married Bisa Hall on June 15, 1999. The purpose of the marriage was to allow Hall, his ex-girlfriend at the time, to qualify for in-state tuition based on Byron's Florida residency. According to Hall, the marriage was not a romantic relationship and she and Donalds did not live together as a married couple.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.thelist.com/2049519/rep-byron-donalds-first-marriage-mess-according-ex-wife/ |title= Rep. Byron Donalds' First Marriage Was An Utter Mess, According To His Ex |first=Carissa Jean |last=Mares |date= March 24, 2025 |access-date=15 February 2026 |archive-date=June 5, 2026 |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20260605142656/https://www.thelist.com/2049519/rep-byron-donalds-first-marriage-mess-according-ex-wife/ |url-status=live }}</ref> They divorced in 2002.<ref>{{cite web |url= https://www.blackenterprise.com/byron-donalds-ex-wife-exposes-past-life-lies/ |title=Byron Donalds' Ex-Wife Exposes Past Life Full Of Lies |first=Sharelle B. |last=McNair |date=July 11, 2024 |website=[[Black Enterprise]] |access-date=August 10, 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://news.wgcu.org/top-story/2024-07-09/trump-vp-hopeful-byron-donalds-ex-wife-shares-her-story-says-what-hes-doing-is-super-dangerous |title=Trump VP hopeful Byron Donalds' ex-wife shares her story, says what he's doing is 'super-dangerous' |first=Bob |last=Norman |date=July 9, 2024 |website=WGCU |access-date=August 10, 2024 |archive-date=August 10, 2024 |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20240810131817/https://news.wgcu.org/top-story/2024-07-09/trump-vp-hopeful-byron-donalds-ex-wife-shares-her-story-says-what-hes-doing-is-super-dangerous |url-status=live }}</ref>

Donalds met and started dating his future wife, [[Erika Donalds|Erika Lees]], in 1999 at Florida State University. They married on March 15, 2003. They have three sons and live in [[Naples, Florida]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ceballos| first=Ana| title=Five questions for State Rep. Byron Donalds| url= https://www.naplesnews.com/story/news/politics/2020/01/10/state-rep-byron-donalds-five-questions-naples-republican/4422583002/ |date=January 10, 2010| access-date=September 5, 2020| website=Naples News| language=en-US|archive-date=August 10, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200810055620/https://www.naplesnews.com/story/news/politics/2020/01/10/state-rep-byron-donalds-five-questions-naples-republican/4422583002/|url-status=live}}</ref> Donalds is a [[born again]] Christian. He says he became born again after communicating with [[God in Christianity|God]] at age 21 while working at [[Cracker Barrel]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Gancarski|first=A.J|title=Byron Donalds says he was born again at Cracker Barrel|url=https://floridapolitics.com/archives/737261-byron-donalds-says-he-was-born-again-at-cracker-barrel/|date=January 10, 2010|access-date=May 8, 2025|website=Florida Politics|language=en-US|archive-date=May 9, 2025|archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20250509034625/https://floridapolitics.com/archives/737261-byron-donalds-says-he-was-born-again-at-cracker-barrel/|url-status=live}}</ref>  

=== Assault allegation ===
In August 2022, Donalds and Kelly Mason (also known as Kelly Lichter), a member of the [[Collier County, Florida|Collier County]] School Board, were recorded in a heated exchange,<ref name="Lichter">{{cite news| url=https://floridapolitics.com/archives/557168-tension-boil-between-byron-donalds-collier-school-board-candidate-in-public-outbursts/|title=Tension boil between Byron Donalds, Collier School Board candidate in public outbursts|last=Ogles|first=Jacob|date=19 September 2022|archive-date=July 11, 2026|access-date=July 31, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260711030751/https://floridapolitics.com/archives/557168-tension-boil-between-byron-donalds-collier-school-board-candidate-in-public-outbursts/|url-status=live}}</ref> while inside of a [[Naples, Florida|Naples]] grocery store.<ref>{{cite news|url= https://www.wptv.com/news/politics/byron-donalds-camp-blasts-assault-lawsuit-as-politically-motivated |last=Saunders|first=Forrest|title=Byron Donalds camp blasts assault lawsuit as 'politically motivated'|work=West Palm Beach TV|archive-date=July 28, 2026|access-date=July 31, 2026|archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20260728230928/https://www.wptv.com/news/politics/byron-donalds-camp-blasts-assault-lawsuit-as-politically-motivated|url-status=live}}</ref> Footage of the incident was published online by NBC-2; while much of the video is inaudible, Donalds can be heard yelling at Mason, "You want to end it? Stop the lawsuits, Kelly. Stop that. How about that?" At the time, Mason told media outlets that Donalds was "threatening me, saying he is going to crush me".<ref name="Lichter"/>

In July 2026, Mason filed a second civil lawsuit against Donalds. In a statement, Mason said that in 2022, Donalds "assaulted me. He must answer for his crimes".<ref name="Russell">{{cite news|last= Russell| first=Ty| url= https://www.wfla.com/news/florida/florida-republican-gubernatorial-candidate-donalds-faces-lawsuit-over-alleged-2022-assault/|title=Florida Republican gubernatorial candidate, Byron Donalds, faces lawsuit over alleged 2022 assault|work=WFLA|date=9 July 2026}}</ref> Mason also said she had been intimidated by Donalds and his wife Erika, a former business partner of Mason, into dropping a previous lawsuit.<ref>{{cite news|last1= Watkins |first1=Tyler |last2=Shaw| first2=Derrick| url= https://www.gulfcoastnewsnow.com/article/cyclospora-outbreak-foods-cdc-data/71836151 |title=Collier County School Board member sues Rep. Byron Donalds over grocery store confrontation|work=Gulf Coast News|date=8 July 2026}}</ref> Donalds denied the allegations and called the second lawsuit a "politically motivated attack".<ref name="Russell"/>

